# =====================================================================
# GENETIC PRIVACY — READ BEFORE EDITING
# =====================================================================
# This repository is PUBLIC. It must never contain genotype data, nor any
# artifact from which genotype data could be reconstructed or an individual
# re-identified.
#
# Why the rules below are this broad: 30-80 independent SNPs are enough to
# uniquely identify a person, and Homer et al. (2008) showed that even
# aggregate allele-frequency summaries can reveal whether a specific
# individual is present in a dataset. "It's only summary output" is not a
# safe assumption. Treat every pipeline output as raw DNA until proven
# otherwise.
#
# Rule of thumb: if a file was produced by touching a real person's
# genotypes, it does not go in git. Ever.
# =====================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. RAW / INPUT GENOTYPE DATA
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendor raw-data exports (AncestryDNA, 23andMe, MyHeritage, FTDNA, ...)
AncestryDNA*.txt
AncestryDNA*.csv
AncestryDNA*.zip
genome_*.txt
genome_*.zip
*_23andMe*.txt
*23andMe*.txt
*MyHeritage*.csv
*FTDNA*.csv
*ftdna*.csv
dna_data*.txt

# Any dedicated input locations
/data/raw/
/data/input/
/dna/
/genomes/
/samples/
input/
incoming/

